{
  "id": "npm-ci-lockfile-drift",
  "title": "npm ci rejects package.json / package-lock.json drift after adding zod",
  "description": "A PR to example-org/notify-service adds \"zod\": \"^3.24.1\" to package.json (plus a new src/schemas/webhook.ts that uses it) but does not commit the regenerated package-lock.json. `npm ci` validates the lockfile against package.json before installing anything and exits with EUSAGE ('Missing: zod@... from lock file'), so lint, typecheck and tests never run and docker-build is skipped. The new zod code is not at fault; the fix is to run `npm install` locally and commit the updated package-lock.json. Expected answers mention the lockfile and zod.",
  "repo": {
    "owner": "example-org",
    "repo": "notify-service"
  },
